id: pm-zzw8bi
title: Bound history-redaction regex cost for SDK embeddings without narrowing JavaScript pattern semantics
description: "Explicit operator-provided history regexes can consume unbounded matching/replacement time in the SDK host. This behavior predates PR #1696: the unchanged sink accepts the equivalent escaped source on main and the leading-slash raw form after the parser repair. Existing scanner triage treats history patterns as authorized operator inputs; no new untrusted boundary or security vulnerability is established by this patch. Add an explicit isolated execution budget as resilience hardening for long-lived SDK embeddings while preserving JavaScript regex semantics and private refusals."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: hardening,history,performance,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-09T13:58:39.780Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T14:01:07.638Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Define an execution budget covering matching and replacement and document its host/runtime semantics; A pathological caller-selected pattern cannot monopolize the SDK host event loop and timeout refuses before history/item writes or locks; Preserve supported JavaScript regex flags and replacement behavior with Node and Bun coverage; Retain bounded isolated-process negative controls for pathological existing and leading-slash forms plus a normal-pattern control
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: SDK embeddings can apply trusted regex redaction with predictable resource bounds and truthful no-write timeout recovery.
